      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the `mm/madvise.c` hunk goes, this becomes a test-only patch, so could the subject and body say so? For example \"ANDROID: P3S: selftests: mm: Test anon VMA naming in 4KB processes\", explaining that `madvise_set_anon_name()` has followed the process page size since \"ANDROID: P3S: mm: madvise: Support 4KB alignment and vector_madvise\" (aosp/4312489).\n\nThe second sentence also reads like a note about an earlier patchset: the /dev/zero split check only arrives in aosp/4367945, and there is no other page size API here to compare with.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c8985db57e870f6038a3cb3cdfea29ef2a57640a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff1f9370_e22fcf61",
        "filename": "mm/madvise.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2222,
