        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this reverts 8d2b747b50f4 (\"ANDROID: 16K: Prevent non-__PAGE_ALIGNED() VMA splits by anon names\") for x86_64 page size emulation: when booted with `page_shift\u003d14`, `__PAGE_MASK` is the emulated 16KB mask there, while without `CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` `mm_pte_mask()` is always the 4KB kernel mask.\n\nOn arm64 I think it doesn\u0027t change anything: outside x86_64, `__page_shift()` is just `PAGE_SHIFT` (`include/linux/page_size_compat_defs.h:47`), and since aosp/4312489 opted `mm/madvise.c` into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, that is `mm_pte_shift(p3s_current_mm())`. The only caller, `set_anon_vma_name()` (called from `prctl_set_vma()`), passes `current-\u003emm` without a remote mm context, so both masks are the same.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this hunk and the `\u003clinux/p3s/mm.h\u003e` include? As far as I can see, `anon_vma_name_ppps` should already pass without them. Did you see it fail?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c8985db57e870f6038a3cb3cdfea29ef2a57640a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
