      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This header adds 491 lines, but as far as I can see this patch and aosp/4367943 only use `PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE`, `NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE` and the re-exec helpers behind `PPPS_COMPAT_MAIN()`. Everything else gets its first user several topics later: `ppps_run_mode()` in aosp/4367960, `exec_native()` and the pagemap and smaps readers in aosp/4367975, and `ppps_geometry_main()`, `read_full()`/`pwrite_full()`, `ppps_status_kb()`, the fixture helpers and `AF_XDP`/`SOL_XDP` in aosp/4367986.\n\nWould you mind moving the header into its own selftests patch with only what its first users need, and letting later patches add helpers together with their first user? That would also keep this patch about anon VMA naming.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c8985db57e870f6038a3cb3cdfea29ef2a57640a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
