      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: could you add a blank line before this comment?\n\n`checkpatch.pl --strict` also asks for `__maybe_unused` (which `kselftest.h` defines) instead of `__attribute__((unused))` on `ppps_argv0`, and for `va_list ap` in `ppps_vexec_or_die()` to line up with the open parenthesis. `NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE` in `anon_vma_name_ppps.c` is one column off as well.\n\nIts warning about the `return` in `PPPS_COMPAT_MAIN()` looks fine to me, since `TEST_HARNESS_MAIN` in `kselftest_harness.h` does the same.",
