      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried that tests using `PPPS_COMPAT_MAIN()` fail rather than skip on kernels without P3S. `personality()` stores any value and exec ignores the bit there, so on a 16KB kernel without P3S the `--run` child is still 16KB and `ppps_require_compat()` calls `ksft_exit_fail_msg()`. On a 4KB kernel, `getpagesize() \u003d\u003d 4096` sends the test straight to `run()`, so it passes without exercising P3S, as the comment above `ppps_geometry_main()` points out.\n\nSince run_vmtests.sh runs `anon_vma_name_ppps` and `madvise_remove_ppps` unconditionally, could this skip in both cases, as `ppps_geometry_main()` does? That is, skip when the `--run` child isn\u0027t 4KB, and when the test starts as a 4KB process without `ADDR_4KB_COMPAT_PAGE_SIZE` in `personality(0xffffffff)`. That\u0027s also the skip I suggested for the AArch32 tests on aosp/4367935.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c8985db57e870f6038a3cb3cdfea29ef2a57640a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
